WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
You enter the room. The reason you came seems to vanish.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:13.000
But did the doorway erase a memory—or change the context?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.500
A 2011 study found forgetting on specific object tests.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:26.000
A 2021 replication showed that task and memory load matter.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
In 2026, researchers even found a brief benefit near some boundaries.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.000
The evidence is more interesting than a magic doorframe.
